VIUA(1) "Viua VM PUT_VIUAVM_VERSION_HERE" "Viua VM Manual"

# NAME

viua - the entry point of the Viua VM toolchain

# SYNOPSIS

*viua* _tool_ [_options_...] [_operands_...]

*viua* [_tool_] *--version* [*--verbose*]++
*viua* [_tool_] *--built-with*

*viua* *--help* [_tool_]++
*viua* [_tool_] *--help*++
*viua* *help* [_tool_]

*viua* *--prefix*

# DESCRIPTION

The frontend script for the Viua toolchain, dispatching commands to internal
executables. For example, the following command

	\]$ viua asm --out foo.o foo.asm

will execute

	/usr/local/libexec/viua/asm --out foo.o foo.asm

if the toolchain has been installed into the /usr/local prefix. The internal
executables can be used directly, but using them through the *viua* frontend is
more convenient.

Why even use a frontend script? To avoit polluting *PATH* with viua-foo,
viua-bar, viua-baz, etc commands; and to allow having multiple Viua versions
installed in parallel.

The following tools are available:

- *asm* - the assembler
- *ld* - the linker
- *vm* - the interpreter
- *dis* - the disassembler
- *readelf* - the ELF inspector

See their respective man pages eg, *viua-asm*(1), for more information.

# OPTIONS

include(common/tool-options.scdoc)

*--prefix*
	Display the currently used prefix.

# EXIT STATUS

|[ 0
:< Successful program execution
|  1
:  Error during program execution

The internal tools report different exit codes and to signal specific
conditions. See their respective man pages for more information.

